WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.951
There once was a boy named Thomas who lived just down the street in the house with the red bricks.

2
00:00:05.952 --> 00:00:11.107
Thomas didn't care about the environment, and he never recycled his garbage.

3
00:00:11.108 --> 00:00:17.075
One day an old wizard smelled an awful stench while he was working in his basement.

4
00:00:17.076 --> 00:00:24.984
He walked upstairs and outside and kept following the scent until he found himself in front of Thomas' house.

5
00:00:24.985 --> 00:00:29.078
He stopped out front and looked at the garbage piled up on the curb.

6
00:00:29.079 --> 00:00:34.009
He shook his head with disgust and said, "Look at all this trash!

7
00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:40.738
Thomas must learn that he should not waste his garbage."

8
00:00:40.739 --> 00:00:45.409
The wizard pulled out his wand and put a spell on Thomas' house.

9
00:00:45.410 --> 00:00:50.325
Now, every time Thomas threw away good garbage, it would talk to him.

10
00:00:50.326 --> 00:00:55.221
The spell would not go away until Thomas stopped wasting his garbage.

11
00:00:55.222 --> 00:01:00.414
That night Thomas noticed a mistake after he printed his homework.

12
00:01:00.415 --> 00:01:04.341
Without thinking he threw the paper into the trash.

13
00:01:04.342 --> 00:01:08.725
"Hey! What are you doing?" said a voice.

14
00:01:08.726 --> 00:01:12.165
"Who said that?" Thomas asked.

15
00:01:12.166 --> 00:01:19.454
It was the paper! "You are wasting me! I am not garbage," it said.

16
00:01:19.455 --> 00:01:24.550
"Yes, you are!" Thomas pointed. "There is a mistake printed on you."

17
00:01:24.551 --> 00:01:28.586
"Look at me. I still have one blank side," said the paper.

18
00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:30.244
"What can I do with that?"

19
00:01:30.245 --> 00:01:33.351
"You could draw a picture. You could write a note.

20
00:01:33.352 --> 00:01:37.208
You could play a game. You could do your math homework."

21
00:01:37.209 --> 00:01:41.899
"Wow! I never thought about it before," said Thomas.

22
00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.254
"Well, you should start thinking about it more often.

23
00:01:45.255 --> 00:01:51.063
I am precious," the paper explained. "A tree had to die to make me.

24
00:01:51.064 --> 00:01:55.774
Don't waste a tree by throwing me away! You must learn to recycle."

25
00:01:55.775 --> 00:02:00.112
The next day Thomas went to the kitchen to make his lunch.

26
00:02:00.113 --> 00:02:03.972
He ate a peanut butter and jelly sandwich with a glass of milk.

27
00:02:03.973 --> 00:02:07.654
Then he put the empty peanut butter jar into the garbage.

28
00:02:07.655 --> 00:02:13.076
"Excuse me! Take me out of here right now!" said the jar.

29
00:02:13.077 --> 00:02:17.036
"Why? You're garbage," said Thomas.

30
00:02:17.037 --> 00:02:21.076
"No, I am not! You can use me for something else."

31
00:02:21.077 --> 00:02:24.102
"Something else? Like what?"

32
00:02:24.103 --> 00:02:29.444
"I can hold your marbles. I can hold your pennies. I can hold your candy.

33
00:02:29.445 --> 00:02:34.256
I can hold many small treasures," the jar answered.

34
00:02:34.257 --> 00:02:37.386
Thomas' head was spinning with ideas.

35
00:02:37.387 --> 00:02:42.641
This was the strangest thing that had ever happened to him. Talking garbage!

36
00:02:42.642 --> 00:02:48.480
But he agreed that the jar was very useful, so he put it in a safe place.

37
00:02:48.481 --> 00:02:56.098
Later that day, Thomas ate some oranges and threw the orange peels into the trash can. It happened again.

38
00:02:56.099 --> 00:03:02.202
This time the peels started to talk. "Stop! We do not belong in here."

39
00:03:02.203 --> 00:03:07.660
"Why not? You're definitely garbage!" said Thomas.

40
00:03:07.661 --> 00:03:12.890
"There is no way I can reuse you. You would smell bad."

41
00:03:12.891 --> 00:03:15.644
"No, we are very special garbage.

42
00:03:15.645 --> 00:03:18.994
We go into the compost bin," said the peels.

43
00:03:18.995 --> 00:03:22.321
"What is a compost bin?" asked Thomas.

44
00:03:22.322 --> 00:03:27.242
"A compost bin is a special box where you put all your vegetable and fruit scraps.

45
00:03:27.243 --> 00:03:32.675
In the spring, you put us into your garden, and we help your flowers grow."

46
00:03:32.676 --> 00:03:40.360
Thomas did not understand why his garbage was talking all of a sudden, but he started to understand what it was saying.

47
00:03:40.361 --> 00:03:45.546
He took the orange peels out of the trash can and put them into the compost bin.

48
00:03:45.547 --> 00:03:52.420
The next morning, while Thomas was getting dressed, he accidentally ripped his shirt as he pulled it over his head.

49
00:03:52.421 --> 00:03:57.090
Since it was an old shirt, he took it off and threw it into the garbage.

50
00:03:57.091 --> 00:04:00.315
"Where am I going?" asked the shirt.

51
00:04:00.316 --> 00:04:04.532
"You are an old ripped shirt, so you are going into the garbage.

52
00:04:04.533 --> 00:04:09.088
I'm sorry, but there is nothing I can do with you," said Thomas.

53
00:04:09.089 --> 00:04:15.326
"You are wrong, Thomas! You can use me as a rag. I can wash the floor.

54
00:04:15.327 --> 00:04:18.799
I can clean your bike," explained the shirt.

55
00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:27.409
Thomas was amazed. It seemed that everything that used to be garbage still had a job to do─even orange peels and ripped clothes!

56
00:04:27.410 --> 00:04:30.295
He had a whole new understanding of his trash.

57
00:04:30.296 --> 00:04:33.238
Thomas learned a lot from the talking garbage.

58
00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:36.768
He did not want to cause environmental problems anymore.

59
00:04:36.769 --> 00:04:41.569
That afternoon he went around the house and looked in all of the garbage bins.

60
00:04:41.570 --> 00:04:48.045
He found everything that he could reuse and put it all in a special place with the rest of his treasures.

61
00:04:48.046 --> 00:04:51.663
The next week Thomas' garbage bag was very small.

62
00:04:51.664 --> 00:04:55.138
Even the garbage man was impressed when he came to pick it up.

63
00:04:55.139 --> 00:05:01.713
Thomas had saved all of the used paper, all of the empty bottles, and all of his old clothes.

64
00:05:01.714 --> 00:05:05.255
He had even made compost out of his fruits and vegetables!

65
00:05:05.256 --> 00:05:07.734
There was hardly anything to throw away.

66
00:05:07.735 --> 00:05:13.534
However, the garbage man was not the only person who was amazed by Thomas' new habit.

67
00:05:13.535 --> 00:05:18.432
The old wizard had also seen the small bag of garbage on the curb that day.

68
00:05:18.433 --> 00:05:24.646
During the night, when everyone was asleep, he walked by Thomas' house enjoying the fresh air.

69
00:05:24.647 --> 00:05:27.608
He smiled and laughed as he looked toward the house.

70
00:05:27.609 --> 00:05:31.008
"Ha-ha! Thomas, you have learned your lesson.

71
00:05:31.009 --> 00:05:36.863
You have learned to save your garbage, so I will remove the spell from your house."

